cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Agnostos in research or a report, please cite it as below."
title: "Agnostos: resume-driven academic outreach for research internships"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Avinash Chandra
    family-names: Gupta
    alias: Avinashistoocool
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Avinashistoocool/Agnostos-v2"
url: "https://avinashistoocool.github.io/Agnostos-v2/"
abstract: >-
  Agnostos is an open-source command-line tool that helps students find research internships.
  It parses a resume, builds a professor list from a research topic via the OpenAlex works index
  (first/last authors, relevance floor, field anchoring, seniority gate) or reads an existing
  spreadsheet, ranks it locally with a TF-IDF cosine plus a saturating domain-term bonus, enriches
  each professor with recent first/last-author papers, and makes one language-model call per
  professor for an acceptance estimate and a short honest email. Drafts pass through a
  deterministic deslop stage and a rule-based AI-tell score with a conditional rewrite. Addresses
  are verified by DNS and name matching and repaired from the professor's own pages. Mail is sent
  with throttling inside recipient-local working hours, and replies are tracked over IMAP with
  drafted follow-ups.
keywords:
  - academic outreach
  - research internship
  - cold email
  - OpenAlex
  - large language models
  - TF-IDF
  - email verification
  - Groq
